# The drum machine (cavekit-flash.md R7): a toy sequencer that plays by itself; each tap brings players on. The
# place where the left drummers stand is empty before the taps and drawn after them, and the machine sounds at the
# output sink across the taps.
id: flash-app-drums
section: Flash
item: A Flash app does its task, the drum machine: tapped, its players come on (their place empty before, drawn after) and it plays at the output sink
shells: enyo mochi mojo
page: http://192.168.1.245:8097/title/drum-machine
kit: cavekit-flash.md R7
wait rect m 40
wait still m@900,450:60,300,260,430 40
expect flash-drawn m@900,450:60,300,260,430 no
sample empty m@900,450:60,300,260,430
sound-watch 9000
stage-tap m 900 450 454 100
pause 2500
stage-tap m 900 450 169 352
pause 2500
stage-tap m 900 450 454 272
wait differs m@900,450:60,300,260,430 empty 8
expect sound-watched heard
expect flash-drawn m@900,450:60,300,260,430 yes
shoot players
